================================================================================
PATH 1 increment 4: MPI-parallelise the O(N^2) FPOLY2 start-up loop (start.f)
================================================================================
Date     : 2026-06-07
Branch   : mpi-parallel
Binary   : GPU2/run_versions/nbody7b.mpi-cpu  (pure-MPI, OMP_NUM_THREADS=1)
Harness  : mpi_design/poc_validation/scale_split.py  (min-of-2, np={1,2,4,8})
Inputs   : input_gen_N13049_eq , input_gen_N50000_eq  (equal-mass generated Plummer)

WHAT CHANGED
  GPU2/start.f         : the per-particle FPOLY2(I,I,0) start-up loop over
                         [IFIRST,NTOT] is now split across MPI ranks. The loop
                         is order-dependent ONLY through STEPS scaling
                         F->0.5F and FDOT->ONE6*FDOT (read by later particles'
                         derivative sum); each rank reproduces the exact serial
                         F/FDOT state for its block by pre-applying that scaling
                         to all particles BELOW its block, then integrates its
                         block in ascending order. Per-particle results
                         (F,FDOT,X0,D2,D3,D2R,D3R,T0,T0R,STEP,STEPR,TNEW) are
                         Allgathered. NRANKS=1 -> original serial/OpenMP loop.
  GPU2/mpi_nbody.f     : + NBODY_FPOLY_RANGE (static contiguous block split,
                         NSTART..NEND), NBODY_FPOLY_GATHER (12 Allgatherv).
  GPU2/mpi_nbody_stub.f: + no-op stubs (serial / AMUSE builds unchanged).

KEY RESULT: bit-identical to single-rank serial for np=1/2/4/8 at both N, and
the formerly serial FPOLY2 share of start-up now parallelises.

