  bit-identity across np [1,2,4,8]: PASS

INTERPRETATION
  * Integration-only speedup unchanged vs the pre-change baseline
    (np8 3.62-3.73x, p~0.83-0.85) -> the force-decomposition integration path
    is untouched, as intended.
  * start-up at N=50000: 38s (np1) -> 31s (np8), and it now FALLS with np.
    The pre-change baseline (results_N_scaling_2026-06-06.log) had start-up
    RISING to 43-44s at np8 from replicated FPOLY2 + overhead. Raw in-code
    wall np8 speedup improved 1.66x -> 2.04x at N=50000 purely from this.
  * The ~31s plateau at np>=4 is the SERIAL remainder of start-up: FPOLY0
    (the one-shot GPUNB_REGF + GPUIRR_FIRR_VEC initial force/neighbour build,
    O(N^2), still replicated on every rank). FPOLY2 was only ~9s of the 38s.
    => NEXT TARGET (PATH 1b): MPI-decompose FPOLY0 with the SAME existing
       NBODY_REGF_RANGE/GATHER + NBODY_IRRF_GATHER wrappers it already calls
       in intgrt.omp.f. That removes the dominant remaining start-up floor.
